  "description": "FUFWIP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C126 H192 B2 La10 O60. From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La4 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La5 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La6 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La7 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La8 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La9 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La10 (La) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.950-4.505 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.48-116.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C126H192B2La10O60.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
